ing shows a competitive race.", "watch": "A strong Democratic turnout wave in New Jersey, aided by Gov. Sherrill at the top of the ticket, could narrow the margin more than expected.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Jeff Van Drew (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Rep. Jeff Van Drew seeks another term in New Jersey's 2nd District against Democrat Zack Mullock, the Cape May mayor, with a minor independent also on the ballot. The district leans Republican by about five points, and Van Drew holds a large financial advantage, with roughly $895,000 on hand compared with about $105,000 for Mullock. Most expert raters call the race Likely Republican, though a few put it closer, and prediction markets price Van Drew's win probability near 85 percent.\n\nDemocrats have invested in the race, with Gov. Sherrill and other party figures stumping for Mullock, and early voting reports showed Democrats holding a turnout lead even as Republicans led in Election Day voting. Still, the combination of incumbency, the district's lean, and the money gap makes Van Drew a clear favorite, with Mullock needing an unusually strong Democratic environment to close the gap.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1228, "margin": -7.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1056, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0906, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0851, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0722, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1002, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1154, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1407, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1134, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.16, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.159, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem"